+### Resumed after the weekly limit; the e2e "browser crash" was our own timeouts (2026-10-23)
+- **13:04 UTC:** the container had restarted, and the weekly API limit (Oct 17 to Oct 23, 13:00) had stopped every agent.
+  - The checkpoint cron was recreated.
+  - Each lane was checkpointed (05263e8) before anything else.
+  - The e2e gate on e57151f had hit its 90-minute `timeout` after 792 tests.
+- **Root cause of the "crashes"** ([qa-suite-beta](qa-suite-beta.md) T-12): Chromium never crashed. Playwright 1.56 handles SIGTERM and SIGHUP by closing the browser without exiting. Any of these closed the browser mid-run, and every later test then failed with "browser has been closed":
+  - the gate's own `timeout 5400`, which both Oct 17 runs hit (exit 124);
+  - the Bash tool's 2-hour limit on background commands;
+  - a stopped session.
+  - Reproduced with `kill -TERM`. Memory stayed flat at about 200 MB for the browser process, with 12+ GB free.
+- **Changes:**
+  - 9fa0ab2: the runner relaunches a closed browser, so one close fails at most two tests.
+  - The gate runs detached (`setsid nohup`) with a 3-hour limit.
+  - qa-suite-beta's runner patch replaces the relaunch: the runner stops cleanly on a signal, with a partial summary, and relaunches only on a real disconnect.
+  - The gate script archives old logs instead of deleting them. Its old `rm -f gate/*.log` deleted two saved run logs; their facts are in this log.
+- **The batch on 5c0cda3** (gate running):
+  - fix-phone-sizes' second set: M-48, M-49, M-51, M-52 and the 932x430 size;
+  - fix-qa4: D-47 to D-50 and D-52;
+  - qa-desktop-beta-4's pass and its QA section;
+  - fix-density's legend rule (phones only, D-51).
+- **New lanes:**
+  - fix-mr-3: MR-21, MR-22, MR-26, MR-29, MR-33, MR-37 to MR-41, and T-17 (titles with line breaks).
+  - qa-suite-beta, with findings so far:
+    - T-1: three board lists missed Amazon and Meta;
+    - T-4: links.e2e.js was never registered;
+    - T-12: above;
+    - T21 and S-6 root causes;
+    - sharding to about 31 minutes per shard.
+- **fix-qa4:** resumed on UX-51, UX-50 and MR-35.
